  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Higher Ground (7)** (2 other sources): Uploader lists a crowded stage here: Kraz, Karl, Ryan, Deitch, Nick, Ivan and Ian Neville, Bloom, Jennifer and Nikki Glaspie; Uploader lists a large lineup including Ivan and Ian Neville, Nick Daniels, Eric Bloom, Jennifer and Nikki Glaspie [1][2]\n- Reviewer believes song 5 is Nubian Lady, which Yusef Lateef played and Kenny Barron likely composed [3]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **flip it up**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n- **Higher Ground (7)**: earliest performance in the archive; mythic rare: 2 archived performances [4]\n- **Move On Up (10)**: rare: 11 archived performances [4]\n- **Sing a Simple Song (11)**: mythic rare: 2 archived performances [4]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **rfa2011-08-14.akg483.flac16** (recommended): source not stated; 4 songs; 122 min; rated 5/5 by 1 [1]\n- **rfa2011-08-14.akg483.flac24**: source not stated; 4 songs; 122 min [2]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Early in the show, Karl Denson joins the trio, followed by Jennifer Hartswick and Shmeeans [2]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **rfa2011-08-14.akg483.flac16**: taped by corey the groundhog (china_c_a_tATyahooDOTcom); transferred by groundhog; source: akg 483 > V2 > r-44 > WAV (24/96k) [1]. Also: Captured with AKG 483 mics through a V2 preamp into an R-44 recorder, at 24-bit/96k; Transferred from WAV through Audacity (down to 44.1k) and xACT to FLAC; taped by corey the groundhog [1]\n- **rfa2011-08-14.akg483.flac24**: taped by corey the groundhog (china_c_a_tATyahooDOTcom); transferred by groundhog; source: akg 483 > V2 > r-44 > WAV (24/96k) [2]. Also: This is a 24-bit version of the recording, not meant for burning to CD [2]",
